Subject: [PATCH 141/148] hjviewer: the admin view in the app's look (UX-S4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U36: the operator's view (hjviewer_admin.dart) leaves default Material for
the 1.7.0 look. Its two tabs are the new HjvPillTabs
(common/widgets/hjv_pill_tabs.dart): pills of text as the PC list's tab bar
draws them, the selected one on primarySoft in primaryStrong at 600, the
others in textSecondary at 400, a screen reader hearing which is selected and
the keyboard's focus ring; they drive the DefaultTabController, so the
TabBarView under them pages as before. On a phone each user and each PC is a
card (hjvCardDecoration, medium radius) 8 apart instead of a divided list,
with the outlined person and desktop icons; whether a user is active stays
the first word of the second line, not the icon. The wide table sits in one
card with border-coloured lines, its header at 12/600 in textTertiary. An
empty list (and a search that finds nothing) is hjvPeersPlaceholder, a failed
request an HjvCallout in the danger tone, the dialog's [닫기] hjvButton. The
texts are W1's (D-17: '관리자' in app texts only), unchanged here.

Tests: hjviewer_style_test.dart checks the pills' colours, weights, height,
semantics and paging. The bridge-needing hjviewer_admin_widgets_test.dart
reads the error through hjvKeepAll (HjvCallout keeps Korean words whole) and
gains a test that an empty list shows the placeholder and a search that finds
nothing its own.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
